## Burner Point production environment variables
## Burner Point environment configuration
## Keep real secrets only in ignored .env files or deployment dashboards.
## .env.example files use NAMES ONLY (no real values).
## - Keep `.env` out of git (already ignored).
## - `.env.example` must contain variable NAMES ONLY (no real values).
## - Public variables may be exposed to the client ONLY when prefixed with
##   `NEXT_PUBLIC_` (web) or `EXPO_PUBLIC_` (mobile).

## =========================================
## Core
## =========================================
NODE_ENV=
APP_NAME=
APP_URL=
API_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

## =========================================
## Database
## =========================================
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=

